B.cno=new A.h1("What is PediAid?","PediAid is a paediatric & neonatal clinical reference app. In one place: 40+ bedside calculators, 676 drugs (Neofax + Harriet Lane) with a structured detail view, growth charts (WHO, IAP, Fenton, INTERGROWTH), bilirubin pathways (AAP 2022 + NICE CG98), IAP STG 2022, IAP Action Plan 2026, NNF CPG 2021, lab references, emergency NICU/PICU drug bundles and acute-care protocols (DKA, RSI, status epilepticus, snake / scorpion envenomation, hypertensive emergency).\n\nRuns on Android, iOS, web and desktop. Works offline once the assets load.")
B.cn8=new A.h1("Who is PediAid built for?","Paediatricians, neonatologists, paediatric / neonatal registrars and fellows, NICU / PICU nurses and final-year medical students. The app assumes the user is a qualified or training healthcare professional.")
B.cnq=new A.h1("Is PediAid a substitute for clinical judgement?","No. PediAid is a clinical decision support tool intended for use by qualified healthcare professionals only. Always verify every dose, threshold and centile against current guidelines, the patient's clinical context and your local protocols before any treatment decision.")
B.cnm=new A.h1("Where does the data come from?",'\u2022 Bilirubin thresholds: AAP 2022 (\u226535 wk) and NICE CG98 (<35 wk).\n\u2022 Growth charts: WHO 2006 / 2007, IAP 2015, Fenton 2013, INTERGROWTH-21st.\n\u2022 Drug formulary: Neofax Nov 2024 (199 NICU drugs, fully cross-checked) + Harriet Lane 22nd edition (478 paediatric drugs, restructured into clean dose blocks).\n\u2022 Indian brand names: IAP Drug Formulary 2024 + DailyMed cross-references.\n\u2022 Standard treatment guidelines: IAP STG 2022, IAP Action Plan 2026, NNF CPG 2021.\n\u2022 Lab references: Harriet Lane chapter 14.\n\nEvery calculator, drug entry and chart names its source on screen. Original PDFs are reachable from inside each drug page via the "Open source PDF" link.')
B.cnc=new A.h1("How are drug doses cross-checked?","Each of the 199 Neofax-derived drugs has every numeric dose fact verified against the source Neofax monograph: 75% are verbatim matches, the remaining 25% are intentional paraphrasing (same numeric value and unit, different surrounding wording \u2014 done to stay copyright-safe). Spot checks across 100+ paraphrased entries found zero numeric or unit errors.\n\nHarriet Lane\u2013derived paediatric drugs are auto-extracted by a structured-section parser, then split into Quick Summary, Dose, Preparation, Monitoring, Common vs Serious adverse effects and Contraindications. Original wording is preserved verbatim \u2014 only the layout changes.")
B.cnf=new A.h1("How accurate are the calculators?","The math is verified against the source publication for every tool. Formulas are visible on every result screen so you can re-check the calculation yourself. If you find a discrepancy, report it via Settings \u2192 Report a bug \u2014 we read every report.")
B.cne=new A.h1("How do I find a specific drug, calculator or guideline?",'Tap the search bar at the top of the home screen. Type anything \u2014 drug names, abbreviations, guideline topics \u2014 and results land grouped by category (Calculators, Drugs, Guides, Charts, IAP STG, NNF CPG, Academics).\n\nCommon abbreviations resolve automatically:\n\u2022 "uti" \u2192 urinary tract infection chapter\n\u2022 "dka" \u2192 diabetic ketoacidosis algorithm\n\u2022 "rsi" \u2192 rapid sequence intubation\n\u2022 "2d echo" \u2192 neonatal echo guide + echo calculators\n\u2022 "vanc" \u2192 Vancomycin drug entry\n\u2022 "apap" or "acetaminophen" \u2192 Paracetamol\n\u2022 "ett" \u2192 endotracheal tube size & depth\n\u2022 "uvc / uac" \u2192 umbilical catheter depth\n\u2022 "sga / aga / lga / lbw / vlbw / elbw" \u2192 birthweight classification.')
B.cn7=new A.h1("How do I read a drug's dose page?",'Drug Formulary \u2192 "Drug Formulary 2.0" \u2192 Neonatology or Paediatrics \u2192 tap the drug. The detail page is laid out the same way for every drug:\n\n1. Quick Summary card \u2014 auto-extracted Route \xb7 Key dose \xb7 Infusion \xb7 Max \xb7 Watch for \xb7 Monitor.\n2. Dose \u2014 per indication, per population (Neonate / Infant / Child / Adolescent / Adult), with route chips and bold dose values.\n3. Indian formulations & brands (Neofax drugs).\n4. Preparation \u2014 reconstitution + incompatibilities.\n5. Monitoring.\n6. Common adverse effects (orange) vs Serious toxicities (red \u2014 sentences containing fatal / cardiac arrest / anaphylaxis / Stevens-Johnson / hepatic failure / etc. auto-flagged).\n7. Contraindications & cautions.\n8. Renal / hepatic adjustment.\n9. Notes & pearls.\n\nThe original Neofax / Harriet Lane PDF is one tap away from the bottom of every drug page.')
B.cnp=new A.h1("What's Emergency NICU / PICU Drugs?","A red banner on the Drug Formulary screen leads to crash-cart drug bundles with live weight-based preparation. Enter the patient's weight once and see ready-to-give doses for adrenaline, atropine, naloxone, sodium bicarbonate, calcium gluconate, dextrose 10% and the full PICU pressor / inotrope / sedation infusion list.\n\nFaster than a calculator when seconds matter.")
B.cn4=new A.h1("How do I customise Quick Access?",'On the home screen \u2192 Quick Access section \u2192 tap "Edit". You can add or remove tiles for any combination of calculators and tools. The choice persists on this device and survives app restarts.')
B.cn6=new A.h1("Is my patient data sent anywhere?","No. Anything you type into a calculator (weight, gestational age, lab values, drug doses) is never sent to our servers and is discarded as soon as you close the screen. The drug formulary, calculators, charts and guides all run entirely on-device.")
B.cna=new A.h1("Where is my data stored?","Your preferences (theme, last-used inputs, Quick Access tiles, onboarding flags) live on THIS DEVICE only, in SharedPreferences. They are cleared when you uninstall.\n\nIf you sign in (when account login is enabled), your email and display name live on our backend at pediaid-backend.onrender.com (Render + Neon Postgres). See the Privacy Policy for full detail.")
B.cnj=new A.h1("Do I need an account to use PediAid?","No. Calculators, charts, drug formulary, growth charts, guides and emergency tools all work without an account, and always will.\n\nYou only need to sign in for the things that are tied to you personally \u2014 the Academics module (peer-reviewed chapters, CME tracking, contributor features), submitting a CME event, or posting to Never Again and following what happens to it.")
B.cnk=new A.h1("Which sign-in should I use \u2014 Google or Apple?","Whichever you already have. On Windows and Android you will see Google; on iPhone, iPad and Mac you will see both.\n\nUse the same one every time. They are separate accounts even if the email looks identical, so signing in with the other button creates a second, empty account rather than opening your existing one \u2014 and PediAid will tell you so rather than silently merging them.")
B.cnb=new A.h1("How do I create an account?","There is no separate sign-up. Tap Sign in and choose Continue with Google, or Continue with Apple on an iPhone or iPad \u2014 your account is created the first time you do. Nothing to fill in, and no verification email to wait for.")
B.cn9=new A.h1("I forgot my password.","PediAid has no password to forget. You sign in with your Google or Apple account, so those handle security and recovery. If you cannot get into that account, recover it with Google or Apple first and PediAid will let you straight back in.")
B.cni=new A.h1("How do I sign out / delete my account?","Settings \u2192 Danger zone \u2192 Sign out (you can sign back in any time) or Delete account (you'll be asked to type DELETE; deletion is immediate and permanent \u2014 no soft-delete, no grace period; all your data is removed from our servers).\n\nYou are never asked for a password to delete \u2014 there isn't one. If you signed in a while ago, Google or Apple may ask you to confirm it is really you first.")
B.cn5=new A.h1("How do I see the tutorial again?","Settings \u2192 Help & Support \u2192 Replay tutorial. This resets BOTH the 6-slide welcome onboarding (Welcome \u2192 Calculators \u2192 Drug Formulary \u2192 Emergency \u2192 Guidelines \u2192 Search) AND the 6-step coachmark tour over the real home-screen UI (drawer, search bar, Quick Access, Calculators tile, Drug Formulary, Guides). The next app open will replay both.")
B.cng=new A.h1("I'm not getting push notifications on my Samsung / Xiaomi / OnePlus / Vivo / Oppo phone.",'These OEMs aggressively kill background apps to save battery, which breaks push delivery. To fix:\n\n1. Long-press the PediAid icon \u2192 App info.\n2. Battery \u2192 set to "Unrestricted" (Samsung) / "No restrictions" (others).\n3. On Xiaomi / Oppo / Vivo / Realme: open Security app \u2192 Permissions \u2192 Autostart \u2192 enable for PediAid.\n4. On Samsung: Settings \u2192 Battery and device care \u2192 Battery \u2192 Background usage limits \u2192 Never sleeping apps \u2192 add PediAid.\n\nPixel and stock-Android phones don\'t need any of this.')
B.cnn=new A.h1("How do I change the app theme or text size?","Settings \u2192 Appearance \u2192 Light / Dark (your choice persists across restarts). For text size: Settings \u2192 Accessibility \u2192 Text size slider (100% \u2013 150%). The Android system-wide font scale also applies on top.")
B.cnl=new A.h1("How do I share PediAid with a colleague?","Settings \u2192 Help & Support \u2192 Share the app. Sends a message with the Play Store link (or the web app link until the Play Store listing is live).")
B.cnh=new A.h1("How do I rate / review PediAid?","Settings \u2192 Help & Support \u2192 Rate PediAid. Opens Google's native in-app review prompt \u2014 you stay inside the app. On web it opens the Play Store listing.")
B.cnd=new A.h1("I found a bug or want a new feature. How do I report it?","Settings \u2192 Help & Support \u2192 Report a bug (or \u2192 Suggest a feature). The email is pre-filled with your app version, build number, platform and account, so we don't have to ask you back. We read every email.")
